1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
Your nose starts to tickle,

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,020
your eyes squeeze shut,

3
00:00:03,020 --> 00:00:05,600
and your whole body launches whatever was in there

4
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,740
across the room. You see,

5
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:10,720
when dust or germs touch the nerves inside your

6
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:13,700
nose, your brain fires a reflex to blast them

7
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:16,120
out, and the spray can travel up to 26

8
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:18,660
feet. But for about one in four people,

9
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:21,620
just stepping into bright sunlight can make them sneeze,

10
00:00:21,620 --> 00:00:24,580
because scientists think the signals from their eyes get

11
00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:26,900
crossed with the nerves in their nose.

12
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,420
And you should never hold one in.

13
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:31,360
One man pinched his nose and closed his mouth

14
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:32,720
to stop a sneeze,

15
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:34,500
and the pressure tore a hole in the back

16
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:35,440
of his throat.
